From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ziteng Xiao <xiaox@gaymail.cn>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mac80211: allow scan when AP bandwidth covers DFS subbands
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ieee80211_can_leave_ch() rejects every scan request when radar is
required but the driver does not implement pre-CAC. mt76 (MT7981/7986/
7988 platforms) has no pre-CAC support, so with the 5 GHz AP on a
channel whose bandwidth covers DFS subbands (e.g. HE160 @ ch36,
5170-5330 MHz covering the 5250-5350 MHz DFS range), "iw scan" fails
permanently with -EBUSY before the driver is ever called.

Additionally, hostapd fails to clear the per-link cac_started flag
after CAC completes on mt76 ("Can't set DFS state for freq ..."
warnings), leaving a stale flag that also blocks scanning forever,
even across reboots.

Relax ieee80211_can_leave_ch(): drop the regulatory_pre_cac_allowed()
early-return and treat a stale cac_started flag as non-blocking (log
only). CAC itself is unaffected and still runs at AP start.

Reproduced on the official 25.12.6 binary (Netcore N60 Pro, MT7986A).

Fixes: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/issues/26572
Signed-off-by: Ziteng Xiao <xiaox@gaymail.cn>
---
 net/mac80211/scan.c |   17 +++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/net/mac80211/scan.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/scan.c
@@ -607,13 +607,22 @@
 	if (!ieee80211_is_radar_required(local, req))
 		return true;
 
-	if (!regulatory_pre_cac_allowed(local->hw.wiphy))
-		return false;
-
+	/*
+	 * Relax (part 1): allow offchannel scan when the current channel
+	 * width covers DFS subbands. Beacons pause during the offchannel
+	 * scan and radar detection resumes once back on the operating
+	 * channel.
+	 *
+	 * Relax (part 2): a stale cac_started flag (hostapd fails to clear
+	 * it for frequencies inside the 160MHz band) must not block scans
+	 * forever. Log it and allow the scan.
+	 */
 	list_for_each_entry(sdata_iter, &local->interfaces, list) {
 		for_each_valid_link(&sdata_iter->wdev, link_id)
 			if (sdata_iter->wdev.links[link_id].cac_started)
-				return false;
+				wiphy_info(local->hw.wiphy,
+					   "scan-dbg: residual cac_started on link %u, allowing scan\n",
+					   link_id);
 	}
 
 	return true;
